## DESCRIPTION
##   Mean, Standard Deviation, and z Scores
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## Tagged by nhamblet

## DBsubject(Statistics)
## DBchapter(Exploratory data analysis/descriptive statistics)
## DBsection(Summary statistics)
## Date(6/3/2002)
## AUTHOR(Jessie Oehrlein)
## INSTITUTION(Fitchburg State University)
## MLT(stat-des-z-score)
## KEYWORDS('measures','mean','standard deviation','z score')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',   'PGML.pl',
    'randomPerson.pl', 'parserRadioButtons.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);

$p = randomPerson();

@slice = num_sort(random_subset(4, 0 .. 4));
@sub   = ('100m', '200m', '400m', '800m', '1500m')[@slice];

@mean = (
    random(10.8, 11.6, 0.1),
    random(23,   27,   0.25),
    random(49,   60,   0.5),
    random(120,  130),
    random(260,  280)
)[@slice];

@sd = (0.2, 3, 4, 8, 14, 8)[@slice];
@z  = random_subset(4, -1, -0.75, -0.5, -0.25, 0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1, 1.25, 1.5,
    1.75, 2);
@time = map { $mean[$_] + $sd[$_] * $z[$_] } (0 .. 3);

($best, $zmax) = (0, $z[0]);
for (1 .. 3) { ($best, $zmax) = ($_, $z[$_]) if $z[$_] > $zmax; }

$rb = RadioButtons([@sub], $best, labels => 'ABC');

BEGIN_PGML

[$p] has run 4 track distances this year: [$sub[0]], [$sub[1]], [$sub[2]], and [$sub[3]].
The means and standard deviations for the race times in seconds, and [$p->their]
times are given in the table below. Convert [$p]'s score into [`z`]-scores. 

[#
    [.Race.][.Mean.][. Std. Dev. .] [. [$p]'s time .] [. [`z`]-score .]{headerrow => 1}*
    [.[$sub[0]].] [. [$mean[0]] .] [. [$sd[0]] .] 
    [. [$time[0]] .] [. [_]{$z[0]} .]*
    [.[$sub[1]].] [. [$mean[1]] .] [. [$sd[1]] .] 
    [. [$time[1]] .] [. [_]{$z[1]} .]*
    [.[$sub[2]].] [. [$mean[2]] .] [. [$sd[2]] .] 
    [. [$time[2]] .] [. [_]{$z[2]} .]*
    [.[$sub[3]].] [. [$mean[3]] .] [. [$sd[3]] .] 
    [. [$time[3]] .] [. [_]{$z[3]} .]*
    #]{align => '|c|c|c|c|c|', horizontalrules =>1, padding => 0.4}

On which race did [$p] have [$p->their] worst relative time? (Remember that in this case, longer times are worse.) [_]{$rb}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Recall that for a value [`x`] from a data set with mean [`\bar{x}`] and standard deviation [`s`] that the [`z`]-score can be calculated with:
[``` z  = \frac{x-\bar{x}}{s}```]

For the given table, [$p]'s [`z`]-score for each race is

- [$sub[0]]: [`z = [$z[0]] `]
- [$sub[1]]: [`z = [$z[1]] `]
- [$sub[2]]: [`z = [$z[2]] `]
- [$sub[3]]: [`z = [$z[3]] `]

And looking at the largest [`z`] score this occured in the [$sub[$best]] race. 
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();       # This should be the last executable line in the problem.